# Valgrind suppressions for voc's conservative garbage collector.
#
# Heap.GC(TRUE) scans every word of the stack for things that look
# like heap pointers (voc src/runtime/Heap.Mod: MarkStack, then
# HeapSort/Sift and MarkCandidates over the candidates it found),
# including words that were never written. Memcheck reports each such
# read as an uninitialised-value error: TestLiveness, which forces GCs,
# showed 663,006 of them from 18 contexts, all in these four functions
# (confirmed live). That is how a conservative collector works, not a
# bug in the binding.
#
# Only uninitialised-value errors whose TOP frame is one of these
# stack-scan functions are suppressed; the same kinds of error anywhere
# else, and every invalid read/write and leak, are still reported.

{
   voc-gc-markstack-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:Heap_MarkStack
}
{
   voc-gc-markstack-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:Heap_MarkStack
}
{
   voc-gc-heapsort-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:Heap_HeapSort
}
{
   voc-gc-heapsort-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:Heap_HeapSort
}
{
   voc-gc-sift-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:Heap_Sift
}
{
   voc-gc-sift-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:Heap_Sift
}
{
   voc-gc-markcandidates-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:Heap_MarkCandidates
}
{
   voc-gc-markcandidates-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:Heap_MarkCandidates
}
